    "The SMS centre (SMSC) each home network sends texts through, for SIMs whose own number VowiDroid cannot read:",
    "Android lets only privileged apps read it off the phone's SIM, and the iPhone carrier bundles do not carry it.",
    "A line uses the user's own entry first, then the number read from the SIM (cards in a USB reader give it up),",
    "then this table through the carrier profile. Hand-kept: tools/import_carrier_bundles.py never reads or writes it.",
    "Each entry names its source; 'note' says when the source is a carrier community thread rather than a carrier page,",
    "or when a carrier runs a second centre for some plans. home_plmns are MCC+MNC with a two- or three-digit MNC."
